module j3.gfx
    Forward OpenGL 3.3 beside `j3.game`'s 2D renderer.
    One directional sun, one shadow map, per-pixel shade. No voxel types here.
    Entry points come from `game.glProc` (3.3 is not a stable libGL export).
    Main thread only: it needs the GL context (`j3c doc threads`). Only these touch no state and
    may run on a worker: `emitFace`, `emitFaceAo` (mesh building), `boxInClip`, `rayAabb` (geometry),
    `plainSurface`, `fxWidth`.

fn setFov(degrees: f32)
    Vertical field of view in degrees for orbit camera passes and `mouseRay`. `0` restores 60.
fn setOrtho(half: f32)
    Draw orbit camera passes orthographically, `half` world units from the view's center to
    its top edge. `0` switches back to perspective. `mouseRay` follows.
const FACE_NX: int = 0
    Unit cube face -X.

const FACE_PX: int = 1
    Unit cube face +X.

const FACE_NY: int = 2
    Unit cube face -Y.

const FACE_PY: int = 3
    Unit cube face +Y.

const FACE_NZ: int = 4
    Unit cube face -Z.

const FACE_PZ: int = 5
    Unit cube face +Z.

struct Orbit
    Orbit camera around a target point.
    target: Vec3
        Point looked at.
    yaw: f32
        Yaw angle in radians.
    pitch: f32
        Pitch angle in radians.
    radius: f32
        Distance from target.
    fn Orbit.create(target: Vec3, yaw: f32, pitch: f32, radius: f32): Orbit
        Build an orbit camera.
    fn Orbit.eye(this: Orbit): Vec3
        World-space eye position.
    fn Orbit.view(this: Orbit): Mat4
        View matrix looking at the target.
    fn Orbit.orbit(this: &Orbit, dyaw: f32, dpitch: f32)
        Nudge yaw/pitch; pitch is clamped.
    fn Orbit.zoom(this: &Orbit, delta: f32, lo: f32, hi: f32)
        Change radius by delta, clamped to [lo, hi].

struct Look
    First-person look camera (eye, yaw, pitch).
    eye: Vec3
        Eye position in world space.
    yaw: f32
        Yaw in radians (0 looks down -Z).
    pitch: f32
        Pitch in radians.
    roll: f32
        Roll in radians around the view direction; positive leans right. Only `view` uses it.
    fn Look.create(eye: Vec3, yaw: f32, pitch: f32): Look
        Build a look camera (no roll).
    fn Look.forward(this: Look): Vec3
        Unit forward vector from yaw/pitch.
    fn Look.right(this: Look): Vec3
        Horizontal right vector from yaw.
    fn Look.view(this: Look): Mat4
        View matrix from eye looking forward.

struct Ray
    Ray from an origin along a unit direction.
    origin: Vec3
        Start point in world space.
    dir: Vec3
        Unit direction.

struct RayHit
    Distance along a ray to an AABB, or a miss.
    ok: bool
        True when the segment hits the box.
    t: f32
        Distance from the origin to the hit. Zero when the origin is inside.

struct Tex
    RGBA8 texture uploaded for `albedo`.
    id: u32
        OpenGL texture id. Zero when empty.
    w: i32
        Width in pixels.
    h: i32
        Height in pixels.

struct Mesh
    Uploaded triangle mesh (VAO/VBO and vertex count).
    vao: u32 = 0
        Vertex array object id.
    vbo: u32 = 0
        Vertex buffer object id.
    count: int = 0
        Number of vertices.

fn draw(mesh: Mesh, model: Mat4)
    Draw a mesh in the current shadow or camera pass. Opaque, back faces culled.
fn drawDoubleSided(mesh: Mesh, model: Mat4)
    Draw both sides of an opaque mesh, matching glTF double-sided materials.
fn drawHull(mesh: Mesh, model: Mat4)
    Draw only a mesh's back faces, in the camera pass. Drawn a little bigger than the mesh
    with an unlit `gfx.material(zero, color)`, it is an outline that follows the shape.
fn drawCutout(mesh: Mesh, model: Mat4)
    Draw a mesh with alpha below 0.5 discarded and both sides visible.
    The shadow pass discards the same texels, so a card does not cast a solid rectangle.
fn drawRun(meshes: []Mesh, models: []Mat4, n: int, cutout: bool)
    Draw the first `n` meshes, each at its model, all with the current surface and albedo:
    like `draw` (or `drawCutout`) in a loop, but in the camera pass the shader state is set
    once and each later mesh only sets its model. For many meshes sharing one look (terrain).
    The shadow pass batches the same way, except for translucent shadows (`shadowLet`).
fn drawSky(mesh: Mesh)
    Draw `mesh` (an inside-out unit sphere) as the sky: centered on the eye, behind
    everything, without depth. Draw it before the rest of the camera pass.
fn depthBias(level: f32)
    Pull later camera-pass draws `level` steps toward the viewer in depth, so a surface lying
    flush on another (a decal, trim, a road line) wins without being moved. 0 turns it off.
    No-op outside the camera pass, whose shadow offset is its own.
fn drawMark(mesh: Mesh, model: Mat4, color: Vec3)
    Unlit rim in `color`, following the albedo's alpha edge. No-op outside the camera pass.
fn drawAlpha(mesh: Mesh, model: Mat4, a: f32)
    Draw `mesh` with alpha `a`. Values below 1 enable blending for that draw.
fn drawBlended(mesh: Mesh, model: Mat4, a: f32)
    Draw `mesh` blended over what is already drawn, with alpha `a` times the albedo texture's
    alpha. Draw these after opaque meshes, farthest first.
fn plainSurface(): Surface
fn surface(s: Surface)
    Later draws use surface `s` until changed.
fn material(tint: Vec3, glow: Vec3)
    Multiply later draws' albedo by `tint` and add `glow` (unlit light the surface gives
    off), with an otherwise plain surface.
fn cameraEye(): Vec3
    Eye position of the latest camera pass.
fn castShadow(through: Vec3)
    Later shadow-pass draws let `through` of the sunlight past them (per color, 0..1).
    Black, the default, is a solid shadow; anything else is a see-through, tinted one.
fn boxInClip(clip: Mat4, lo: Vec3, hi: Vec3): bool
    Whether the box `lo`..`hi` can reach the clip volume of `clip` (projection × view × model).
    False only when all eight corners are outside one clip plane, so GL would clip it all anyway.
fn visible(model: Mat4, lo: Vec3, hi: Vec3): bool
    Whether a mesh with local bounds `lo`..`hi` drawn at `model` can show in the current pass:
    on screen in the camera pass, inside the light's box in the shadow pass.
fn shadowEpoch(): int
    Counts `shadowPass` calls, so a camera pass can tell which shadow pass it follows.
fn inCameraPass(): bool
    Whether draws now go to the camera (not the shadow map).
const LIGHTS: int = 8
    How many point lights shine at once.

fn light(i: int, pos: Vec3, color: Vec3, radius: f32)
    Set point light `i` (0..7). Radius `0` turns that light off.
fn drawLine(a: Vec3, b: Vec3, color: Vec3)
    Unlit world-space line in the camera pass.
fn drawInstanced(mesh: Mesh, models: []Mat4)
    Draw one copy of `mesh` per matrix with the current surface, in instanced GL draws.
struct Instance
    One opaque instance. Tint and emission replace the current material's colors.
    model: Mat4
    tint: Vec3
    emission: Vec3

fn drawInstances(mesh: Mesh, instances: []Instance)
    Draw colored copies, retaining the current surface's other properties.
    Custom effects use ordinary draws so their existing uniform contract is preserved.
fn drawInstancesAlpha(mesh: Mesh, instances: []Instance, a: f32)
    `drawInstances` with one alpha `a` for the whole batch. Below 1 it blends with depth writes off:
    draw these after the opaque scene; copies are not sorted against each other.
fn drawHullInstances(mesh: Mesh, instances: []Instance)
    Batched back-face outlines, camera pass only.
fn drawInstancedDoubleSided(mesh: Mesh, models: []Mat4)
    `drawInstanced` with back faces drawn too, like `drawDoubleSided`.
fn emitFace(out: []f32, at: int, x: f32, y: f32, z: f32, dir: int, r: f32, g: f32, b: f32, emi: f32): int
    Append six verts for one unit-cube face; returns the next write index.
fn emitFaceAo(out: []f32, at: int, x: f32, y: f32, z: f32, dir: int, r: f32, g: f32, b: f32, emi: f32, s0: f32, s1: f32, s2: f32, s3: f32): int
    Append an AO-shaded unit-cube face; returns the next write index.
fn effectProgram(glsl: string, params: []FxParam, log: &Text, firstLine: &int, vlog: &Text, vertFirst: &int): int
    Compile a material effect: `glsl` (its `effect` hook) with a `uFx_<name>` uniform per
    param, into the stock lit shader. Returns the id for `Surface.fx`, or 0 with the driver's
    errors in `log`. `firstLine` gets the compiled line `glsl` starts on, for mapping errors.
    Effect draws use the plain lit variant: no traced shadows, mirrors, or glass.
    GLSL with an `#ifdef J3_VERTEX` block is also compiled into the vertex shader, with
    `J3_VERTEX` defined; that block defines `vec3 displace(vec3 pos, vec3 normal)` (world
    space, returns the new position). Its errors go to `vlog`, `vertFirst` set like `firstLine`.
    It runs in the shadow map pass too, so displaced meshes cast displaced shadows.
fn postProgram(glsl: string, params: []FxParam, log: &Text, firstLine: &int): int
    Compile a camera effect: `glsl` defines `vec4 effect(vec2 uv)` and can read `uColor` (the
    frame so far), `uDepth`, `uNear`, `uFar`, `linearDepth(uv)`, `uTime`, `uResolution`, and
    its `uFx_<name>` params. Returns the id for `postPass`, or 0 with errors in `log`.
fn postBegin()
    Send the next camera pass into an offscreen target so `postPass` can run camera effects
    over it. Call before the camera pass; finish with `postPass(..., last = true)`.
fn postPass(fx: int, vals: []f32, last: bool)
    Run camera effect `fx` (`postProgram`'s id) over the frame, with its params in `vals`.
    `last` writes to where the camera pass would have gone and puts the view rect back.
fn effectTexture(fx: int, uniformName: string, image: Tex): bool
    Bind an externally owned 2D texture to a material effect's declared sampler.
    Main thread only. Up to four samplers use units 10..13, separate from built-ins.
    Returns false for an invalid effect, missing uniform, or full binding table.
    Passing a zero-id texture clears that sampler; free textures only after unbinding.
fn freeEffect(fx: int)
    Delete effect `fx` (`effectProgram`'s id). Surfaces still naming it draw stock.
struct Surface
    How a surface looks beyond its texture. `plainSurface()` changes nothing.
    tint: Vec3
        Multiplies the albedo.
    glow: Vec3
        Unlit light the surface gives off.
    spec: f32
        Highlight strength, 0..1.
    shine: f32
        Highlight sharpness, 0 (broad) to 1 (pinpoint).
    reflect: f32
        How much it mirrors its surroundings, 0..1: 1 is a mirror at every angle, lower
        values show mostly at grazing angles. Without a tracer it mirrors the sky (or sky box).
    edge: f32
        See-through where the surface faces the camera, solid at its edges, 0..1. Only
        shows on blended draws. With `reflect`, reads as glass or water.
    ior: f32
        Index of refraction; above 1 the surface is glass and bends what's behind it (from
        `grab`). 1.5 is window glass, 1.33 water.
    rough: f32
        Blurs reflections and dulls the sun glint in them, 0..1.
    thickness: f32
        How far light travels through the object, in world units, for glass bending and
        tint. `scene3d` sets it from the object's size.
    cloud: f32
        For glass: how frosted it is, 0 (clear) to 1 (a lit, solid-looking surface).
    uvScale: Vec2
        Texture coordinates are multiplied by this, then offset.
    uvOffset: Vec2
    fx: int
        Shader effect, from `effectProgram`; 0 is none.
    fxVals: [16]f32
        The effect's param values in param order; a color takes three. Start a `Surface` from
        `plainSurface()` rather than a literal, so fields added later don't break it.

const FX_FLOAT: int = 0
    Shader effect param kinds (`.j3fx` `param.<name>=<type>:<default>`).

const FX_INT: int = 1

const FX_BOOL: int = 2

const FX_COLOR: int = 3

const FX_PARAMS: int = 8
    ponytail: 8 params and 16 floats per effect; raise both if an effect needs more.

const FX_FLOATS: int = 16

struct FxParam
    One effect param: uniform `uFx_<name>`, its `FX_*` kind, and its default (a color uses
    all three, the rest `def[0]`).
    name: string
    kind: int
    def: [3]f32

fn fxWidth(kind: int): int
    Floats a param of `kind` takes in `Surface.fxVals`.
fn shadowPass(sun: Vec3, boundsMin: Vec3, boundsMax: Vec3)
    Begin the shadow depth pass for the given sun and world bounds.
fn cameraPass(cam: Orbit, sun: Vec3, sky: Vec3, sunColor: Vec3)
    Begin the lit camera pass from an orbit camera.
fn cameraPassLook(cam: Look, sun: Vec3, sky: Vec3, sunColor: Vec3)
    Begin the lit camera pass from a look camera.
fn cameraPassLookFov(cam: Look, sun: Vec3, sky: Vec3, sunColor: Vec3, degrees: f32)
    Begin the lit camera pass with a game camera's vertical FOV in degrees.
fn ready(): bool
    Whether `init` has run (a GL context exists).
fn init()
    Load GL procs, compile shaders, build the shadow map, and enable depth.
fn shutdown()
    Delete programs and the shadow map; clear ready state.
fn upload(verts: []f32): Mesh
    Upload interleaved verts as a new mesh.
    10 floats per vertex is untextured. 12 is textured, when that length is not also a multiple of 10.
    A length divisible by both is untextured, so voxel faces keep their layout. Use `uploadUv` to force u v.
fn uploadUv(verts: []f32): Mesh
    Upload a `# j3mesh 2` buffer (12 floats per vertex), including lengths also divisible by 10.
fn uploadUvLight(verts: []f32): Mesh
    Upload verts of 14 floats: pos, normal, color, emission, u v, then `sky` and `block` light (0..1 each).
    A material effect reads them as `vLight` (x sky, y block); the stock shader ignores them.
    Meshes uploaded any other way read `vLight = (1, 0)`.
fn updateUv(mesh: &Mesh, verts: []f32)
    Replace a `# j3mesh 2` buffer. Use this when the float count is also a multiple of 10.
fn update(mesh: &Mesh, verts: []f32)
    Replace a mesh VBO contents and vertex count. Stride follows `upload`.
fn free(mesh: &Mesh)
    Delete a mesh VAO/VBO and zero its fields.
fn tex(pixels: []u8, w: i32, h: i32): Tex
    Upload tightly packed RGBA8 pixels. Panics if the buffer is short.
fn texPixelArt(pixels: []u8, w: i32, h: i32): Tex
    Like `tex`, but sampled with hard nearest-texel filtering and no mipmaps: crisp pixel art at any distance.
fn grab()
    Copy what the current camera pass has drawn so far into the texture glass surfaces
    sample (see `Surface.ior`). Call after the opaque draws, before the see-through ones.
struct Traced
    A scene on the GPU for URP tracing, in two levels: meshes with their own BVHs in their
    own space (`traceMeshes`), and the objects placing them with a BVH over their boxes
    (`traceInstances`). Moving objects only redoes the second.
    tris: u32
    nodes: u32
    top: u32
    inst: u32
    count: int
        Objects; 0 means nothing to trace.

fn traceMeshes(t: &Traced, tris: []f32, count: int, nodes: []f32, nodeCount: int)
    Upload mesh triangles (28 floats each: corner, two edges, three corner normals, color)
    and every mesh's BVH nodes (8 floats each, `j3.gfx.bvh` layout, indices absolute) into
    `t`, reusing its textures.
fn traceInstances(t: &Traced, inst: []f32, count: int, top: []f32, topCount: int)
    Upload objects (24 floats each: world-to-object rows, tint+mirror, glow+ior, then
    roughness, opacity, cloud, and the mesh's root node in `traceMeshes`' nodes) and the
    BVH over them (leaves index objects) into `t`.
fn traceUse(t: Traced, bounces: int, samples: int, shadows: bool, near: f32)
    Trace mirrors and glass through `t` in later draws: rays follow up to `bounces`
    surfaces, rough and glass surfaces average `samples` rays, and `shadows` traces sun
    shadows at hits (else the shadow map is used). `traceOff` stops it.
    Trace with `t`. `shadows` traces sun shadows too, where the shadow map is unsure and
    within `near` of the eye (0: everywhere).
fn traceOff()
fn skyImage(image: Tex)
    Mirrors reflect `image` (an equirect sky, as `builtin:sky` maps it) instead of the plain
    sky color. Id 0 goes back to the sky color.
fn updateTex(image: &Tex, pixels: []u8, w: i32, h: i32)
    Replace the pixels of an existing texture while keeping its GL id stable.
fn freeTex(image: &Tex)
    Delete a texture uploaded with `tex`.
fn albedo(image: Tex)
    Bind `image` as the albedo until the next `albedo` or camera pass.
    The camera pass resets the bind to the white texture.
fn setFog(start: f32, end: f32)
    Fog distances used by the next camera pass. Defaults are 40 and 120.
fn setViewRect(x: f32, y: f32, w: f32, h: f32)
    Render later camera passes into a window-pixel rect (top-left origin), e.g. an editor
    viewport between panels. `mouseRay` maps the pointer through the same rect.
    A zero width or height restores the whole window.
fn viewOrigin(): Vec2
    Top-left of the camera-pass rect in window pixels.
fn viewExtent(): Vec2
    Size of the camera-pass rect in window pixels.
fn toScreen(p: Vec3): Vec3
    Window pixel for a world point under the latest camera pass. `z` is the clip-space `w`;
    zero or less means the point is behind the camera and `x`/`y` are meaningless.
struct ViewState
    What `toScreen` and `mouseRay` read from the last camera pass. Save it before drawing a
    second view (a picture-in-picture, say) and put it back after.
    view: Mat4
    proj: Mat4
    eye: Vec3
    x: f32
    y: f32
    w: f32
    h: f32
    fov: f32
    ortho: f32
    near: f32
    far: f32

fn viewState(): ViewState
fn setViewState(s: ViewState)
    Restore a `viewState`. GL state is left alone; the next camera pass sets it.
struct Target
    An offscreen color and depth target: pass `fbo` to `setOutputFbo` to draw a view into it,
    for example to save it with `readPixels`. `freeTarget` releases it.
    fbo: u32
    color: u32
    depth: u32
    w: int
    h: int

fn makeTarget(w: int, h: int): Target
fn freeTarget(t: &Target)
fn readPixels(w: int, h: int, out: []u8)
    Real pixels, not virtual (`game.setVirtualSize` letterbox bars are in them).
    Copy the `w` by `h` pixels at the bottom-left of the camera pass's output (the window, or
    the framebuffer given to `setOutputFbo`) into `out` as RGBA8, top row first, the way
    `j3.gfx.canvas` and PNG files store them. Call it after drawing and before `game.present`.
fn setOutputFbo(id: u32)
    Route the camera pass into an external framebuffer; zero restores the window.
    The caller owns the framebuffer and must attach both color and depth.
fn shadowTexture(): u32
    Shadow depth texture generated by the most recent shadow pass.
fn shadowMatrix(): Mat4
    Light matrix used to project world points into that shadow texture.
fn clearDepth()
    Clear depth mid camera pass, so later draws (a first-person gun) land on top of the world.
fn setClip(near: f32, far: f32)
    Perspective clip planes used by the next camera pass. Defaults are 0.15 and 200.
fn mouseRay(cam: Orbit): Ray
    World ray through the mouse for an orbit camera. Same fov as the camera pass.
fn mouseRayLook(cam: Look): Ray
    World ray through the mouse for a look camera. Same fov as the camera pass.
fn rayAabb(origin: Vec3, dir: Vec3, lo: Vec3, hi: Vec3, reach: f32): RayHit
    First hit of the ray against an AABB, within `reach`. A miss has `ok == false`.
    An origin inside the box hits at `t == 0`.
